  "details": "I propose a potential option and/or solution to the current problem of ripping, and re-uploading of avatars. By adding an optional whitelist system that allows the user to decide who gets to see their uploaded avatars.\nThe idea is that with the whitelist active, the server itself would deny any download requests \"of your uploaded avatar ID's\" from any user that is not on the whitelist. Meaning publicly shared avatars will still be downloaded, and shown as usual. Unless for example. You are using your friends public avatar, but they also have the whitelist active.\nHaving this would in theory be a reliable way of keeping avatars safe from any would be rippers, and automated ID grabbers. As the simple fact is that if the rippers can not get a hold of your avatar through some download in the first place. Then there will be no ripping to be had.\nSo I believe this feature would help combat this problem fairly well.",
